Theorem TF-2: Variable binding transfer is transparent identity

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `Let { Var(v) }` per Annex E §AIMS TF-2
    - `state(v)` is `v`'s current AimsState in the per-function state map
    - Identity function on AimsState: f(s) = s

  Soundness property:
    Forall s in AimsState. transfer_tf2(Let { Var(v) }) where state(v) = s
    yields dst.state = s (transparent alias).
    L-6 layer (b) monotonicity: forall a, b in AimsState. a ≤ b ⟹ f(a) ≤ f(b).

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) Identity preservation — TF-2 specifies `dst.state := state(v)`;
          no per-dimension transformation. Both SCALAR and non-SCALAR inputs
          pass through unchanged.
      (b) Monotonicity of identity — the identity function id(s) = s is
          monotone on every partial order by definition: a ≤ b ⟹ a ≤ b
          (the conclusion IS the hypothesis).

    Part (a) — input enumeration:
      SCALAR input: id(SCALAR) = SCALAR — sentinel preserved.
      Non-SCALAR input: id(state) = state on all 7 per-dimension carriers
        (Access x Consumption x Cardinality x Uniqueness x Locality x Shape
        x Effect = 14,400-state product per Annex E §AIMS carriers).
      Representative finite enumeration discharged on 3 pair samples:
        - (FRESH(ReusableStruct), CONSERVATIVE) — fresh ≤ conservative
        - (FRESH(CollectionBuffer), FRESH(CollectionBuffer)) — reflexive
        - ((Borrowed, Linear, Once, Unique, BlockLocal, NonReusable, NONE),
           CONSERVATIVE) — borrow ≤ conservative

    Part (b) — monotonicity:
      For any partial order ≤ and identity function id: a ≤ b ⟹ id(a) ≤ id(b)
      ⟺ a ≤ b ⟹ a ≤ b. Tautological.
      Concrete enumeration: for each (a, b) pair in part (a), verify
        product_le(transfer_tf2(a), transfer_tf2(b)) = Some(true).
      Engine confirms via product-lattice componentwise comparison on the
      7 carriers (5 totally-ordered + Shape flat + Effect componentwise-OR).

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) identity-function discharge per
        section_04::verify_tf2_var_alias — identity preserves ≤ trivially)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — input-shape enumeration: SCALAR + non-SCALAR
        sample pairs per section_04::verify_tf2_var_alias)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; product-order primitives
        discharged at L-1..L-6 layer (a) in §02)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-6 / TF-6a only)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-2 via identity-function preservation + product-order componentwise check
